block-classification tables written directly in `blocks/tables.py` (the game
version, the counts in effect and the known deviations are stated as constants in that file). They are a factual classification we chose, derived from
official collision-shape dumps; the dumps themselves, and any Minecraft
textures, models, or game files, are NOT included in this distribution and never
should be. Mojang's usage guidelines define "our assets" as "the code, software,
graphics, textures, images, models, sounds and other audio" and say "do not
redistribute our games or any alterations of our games or game files"; the EULA
says "you may develop tools, plug-ins and services as long as they do not seem
official or approved by us". This package is such a tool. If a future version
needs a larger table, the line to hold is the same one: ship the classification,
not the dump.
